AlohaMini ROS2 bridge
Source package: alohamini_ros2/src/alohamini_lerobot_bridge
File: alohamini_lerobot_bridge/protocol.py
Package license: Apache-2.0

ros2/src/alohamini_camera migrates setup/launch files, camera_node.py,
camera_info.py, protocol.py and extrinsics_node.py from
alohamini_ros2/src/alohamini_camera (Apache-2.0).
Topics, optical frame names, RGB publication, clock selection and the
mount-to-optical transform convention are retained. Changes: native Host
session handling, demand-based camera selection, bounded polling, unified
workspace calibration paths, reviewed-parameter checks and explicit quaternion
ordering. Robot-specific candidate calibration files are not packaged.
docs/ros2.md adapts the source camera package's operational instructions.

src/alohamini/calibration/encoder.py and calibration/lift.py adapt the
JointMapper physical conversions from this ROS2 bridge. Changes include
explicit SI interfaces, validated per-device parameters, explicit stream
continuity reset, and separation of display clamping from physical feedback.

Adaptations: immutable model descriptions; explicit SI units and scalar
validation; standard-library omni-base kinematics; typed command identity
and Host-session-bound ownership without anonymous-command fallback.

AlohaMini robot description assets
Source package: alohamini_ros2/src/alohamini_description
Package license: Apache-2.0
Destination: models/alohamini2pro/{urdf,meshes,config}
Model-local mesh paths replace ROS package URIs. Geometry, joint values,
and mesh bytes are retained. Per-file origins and checksums are recorded
in models/alohamini2pro/provenance.json.

src/alohamini/hardware/feetech.py adapts the STS feedback register layout and
sign-magnitude decoding from src/lerobot/motors/feetech/feetech.py and tables.py.
Changes: read-only serial ownership, monotonic transaction deadline, reception
in arrival order, preserved packet error flags and partial feedback batches.

src/alohamini/runtime/current_protection.py and lifecycle.py adapt overload
timers, command-watchdog sequencing and cleanup from AlohaMini alohamini.py
and alohamini_host.py. Changes: ampere units, explicit lifecycle state,
latched faults, per-device cleanup attempts and no library-level process exit.

src/alohamini/hardware/feetech_device.py adapts motor register addresses,
model numbers, signed goal encoding and grouped target writes from the LeRobot
Feetech driver and AlohaMini Host. Changes: exclusive bounded serial access,
read-only configuration checks, per-motor stop/disable verification, explicit
calibrated joint targets and no implicit EEPROM unlock or torque enable.

src/alohamini/runtime/arm_contact.py adapts AlohaMini's joint stall and gripper
contact limiters from alohamini.py. Changes: calibrated radian/ampere inputs,
explicit release/stroke calibration and failure propagation on missing feedback.
arm_control.py integrates these limits into feedback-driven Host supervision.

src/alohamini/runtime/base_control.py adapts proportional wheel saturation from
AlohaMini._body_to_wheel_raw. lift_control.py adapts LiftAxis encoder accumulation
and height control, adding explicit session-bound reference/continuity checks,
SI interfaces and failure propagation instead of missing-feedback fallbacks.
base_lift_control.py runs these components inside Host feedback supervision.

src/alohamini/client.py adapts the bounded observation request window and
PUSH command transport from AlohaMiniClient and ROS2 ZmqHostTransport.
Changes: framework-independent payloads, strict response validation, lazy
command connection, explicit snapshot-linked session/epoch and no command
age cutoff based solely on policy inference duration. Original wire units
are preserved; transport submission does not acknowledge physical execution.

src/alohamini/calibration/servo.py and runtime/startup.py adapt the deployed
MotorCalibration JSON fields and AlohaMini configure/connect register settings.
Startup verifies installed calibration, prepares both buses with torque disabled,
and enables only after replacing stale targets. hardware/camera.py and
runtime/host.py adapt OpenCV capture, JPEG transport and recording camera cursors
from LeRobot camera_opencv.py and AlohaMini alohamini_host.py/camera_buffer.py.

src/alohamini/runtime/camera_stream.py migrates the AlohaMini camera_stream.py
publisher and its three-part standard-JPEG protocol. Topic names, color conversion
and clock conversion are retained. Changes: capture-worker encoding on subscriber
demand, paired encoded snapshots, bounded subscription processing and shutdown,
and Host-session metadata. The existing 5556 image path remains unchanged.

docs/alohamini.md adapts the hardware introduction, model reference and device
setup instructions from docs/alohamini/{alohamini,profiles,commands}.md in the
LeRobot / AlohaMini source above. Commands refer to the native platform entry points.

src/alohamini/apps/teleop_monitor.py is migrated from examples/alohamini/teleop_monitor.py
with native payload inputs; output formatting, grouping and cadence are retained.
hardware/leader.py and apps/teleoperation.py adapt SOLeader/BiSOLeader calibration and
position mapping, KeyboardTeleop input and AlohaMiniClient keyboard targets.
Host timing aggregation and --profile_timing parsing derive from alohamini_host.py;
grouped bus I/O and asynchronous camera work are reported in their actual scopes.

src/alohamini/apps/visualization.py is migrated from
src/lerobot/utils/rerun_visualization.py with native snapshot/JPEG inputs and
without LeRobot imports. Images are logged as temporal data, and late-arriving
camera streams extend the view layout. apps/teleoperation.py retains the camera
request accumulator and per-cycle pacing from examples/alohamini/teleoperate_bi.py.

src/alohamini/calibration/procedure.py adapts SOLeader.calibrate,
AlohaMini.calibrate and MotorsBus.record_ranges_of_motion. Terminal prompts,
range tables, half-turn offsets, wrist-roll ranges and JSON fields are retained.
Calibration register operations in hardware/feetech_device.py adapt
FeetechMotorsBus.write_calibration and MotorsBus.set_half_turn_homings.
Changes: separate torque-off calibration sessions, verified and relocked EEPROM
writes, restoration attempts on failure, local atomic JSON replacement with
backups, and no automatic motion or lift homing from calibration entry points.

src/alohamini/apps/recording.py migrates StateSampleBuffer, FreshCameraGate and the
multirate observation/input/command/pairing sequence from
examples/alohamini/record_utils_multirate.py, and episode controls/countdown
from record_bi.py and utils/keyboard_input.py. datasets/native.py retains the feedback
field names, order and validity encoding from robots/alohamini/motor_feedback.py.
The local writer adapts asynchronous image writing and recoverable episode
commit behavior from datasets/image_writer.py and dataset_writer.py. Changes:
bounded submissions, native Parquet files and indexed Host JPEG TAR shards
without LeRobot or Hub imports, per-episode journals and recoverable discard.

src/alohamini/apps/replay.py adapts the named-action mapping, absolute frame
schedule, FPS/speed controls and console output from examples/alohamini/replay_bi.py,
and protection-event checks from examples/alohamini/evaluation_safety.py.
Changes: native/local-export action reads without LeRobot or Hub imports,
installed-calibration checks, Host command acceptance acknowledgements,
feedback-supervised target renewal and lease-bound measured-stop cleanup.

src/alohamini/datasets/tools.py adapts numeric feedback, validity-mask and
physical capture-time checks from scripts/check_lerobot_dataset_integrity.py.
Error codes and the separation of structural validity from training review
are retained. Storage traversal targets native Parquet/image episodes; recovery
retains complete journal prefixes in a new dataset. Export preserves JPEG bytes
or losslessly compresses version-1 PNGs without changing numeric rows or safety
sidecars. datasets/images.py centralizes indexed image reads and Host RGB decoding.

src/alohamini/datasets/lerobot_tools.py migrates the existing
scripts/check_lerobot_dataset_integrity.py and repair_lerobot_video_gaps.py.
The metadata-first repair sequence and conservative error classification are
retained, with local statistics helpers from compute_stats.py and utils.py,
bounded image batches, contained file references and source-preserving outputs.
datasets/video.py adapts video_utils.encode_video_frames and
dataset_tools._keep_episodes_from_video_with_av for offline MP4 previews and
range repacking without LeRobot imports. Source images and numeric samples
remain authoritative; previews use the same decoded RGB and frame order.

src/alohamini/datasets/lerobot.py retains RunningQuantileStats from
src/lerobot/datasets/compute_stats.py. Metadata, episode boundaries, task
tables and Arrow feature mappings follow LeRobotDatasetMetadata and
datasets/feature_utils.py, checked against the LeRobot 0.4.4 release.
Changes: direct offline Parquet writing without LeRobot/Hub runtime imports,
embedded PNGs, bounded batches, selected state assembly and source-field
retention. StateSelection in datasets/native.py scales velocity in the recorded Host
position coordinate and converts reported current from mA to A.

examples/debug/{motors,test_cuda,test_cv,test_dataset,test_input,test_mic,
test_network}.py derive from the same-named LeRobot / AlohaMini debug scripts.
The motor table retains its column layout, raw position/offset values, current
conversion and refresh rendering. Its serial access is read-only, exclusive
and deadline-bounded using the native packet transport; missing fields and
servo error flags are reported without modifying torque or EEPROM.
Other diagnostics use native local paths, Parquet and explicit network/model
inputs, with guarded command entry points and resource cleanup.
The separate motor maintenance commands adapt configure_motor_id,
configure_motor_phase and reset_motors_torque from the same source file.
Changes: explicit single-motor EEPROM operations, model/identity checks,
torque-off verification, write readback, relocking after errors and one serial
connection across ID changes. They do not enable torque or change motor modes.

src/alohamini/hardware/find_cameras.py adapts lerobot_find_cameras.py and
OpenCVCamera.find_cameras from src/lerobot/cameras/opencv/camera_opencv.py.
Device labels, metadata and snapshot naming are retained. Local V4L2 discovery
has bounded worker lifetimes; capture reuses native camera workers. Standard
RGB snapshots are stored in new workspace directories without GUI dependencies.

src/alohamini/hardware/find_port.py adapts
src/lerobot/scripts/lerobot_find_port.py. The unplug/Enter/compare workflow and
result messages are retained. Port enumeration uses pyserial without symlink
aliases or serial connections; missing/ambiguous results remain errors, and
interrupted checks also remind the operator to reconnect the USB cable.
